WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:13.101
Tom Becky had lost track of time.

2
00:00:14.082 --> 00:00:16.944
Their candles had gone out, and they both had fallen asleep.

3
00:00:17.705 --> 00:00:18.626
Had they slept long?

4
00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:19.867
Tom wondered.

5
00:00:20.427 --> 00:00:21.648
There was no way of knowing.

6
00:00:21.668 --> 00:00:25.031
"I'm so hungry," said Becky.

7
00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:28.074
"Here." Tom passed her some cake.

8
00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.196
"I saved this for you."

9
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.641
"Are people looking for us?"

10
00:00:35.161 --> 00:00:35.802
asked Becky.

11
00:00:35.822 --> 00:00:38.203
"Sure," said Tom.

12
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:42.806
But he knew the cave was big, and if he and Becky waited to be found, they might

13
00:00:42.866 --> 00:00:43.546
wait forever.

14
00:00:43.566 --> 00:00:47.408
"I think I should explore," he said.

15
00:00:47.428 --> 00:00:51.070
"Here, hold one end of this kite string.

16
00:00:52.431 --> 00:00:56.893
I will go down these side passages as far as I can, and then I'll come back."

17
00:00:58.474 --> 00:01:01.076
Becky was scared, but she agreed to Tom's plan.

18
00:01:02.068 --> 00:01:05.910
Tom crawled slowly into the dark, feeling in front of him like a blind man.

19
00:01:06.571 --> 00:01:09.112
He had only gone a short distance when he heard something.

20
00:01:09.993 --> 00:01:13.375
He gave a shout, and his voice echoed eerily throughout the cave.

21
00:01:15.296 --> 00:01:16.156
Then a light appeared.

22
00:01:17.297 --> 00:01:20.679
When Tom saw who was holding the light, he almost shouted again.

23
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.681
The face in the light was Injun Joe's!

24
00:01:24.601 --> 00:01:26.963
Injun Joe looked just as scared to see Tom.

25
00:01:27.743 --> 00:01:28.844
He bolted away from him.

26
00:01:31.776 --> 00:01:34.877
When Tom crawled back to Becky, she asked him why he had shouted.

27
00:01:34.897 --> 00:01:38.258
"Just for luck," said Tom.

28
00:01:38.958 --> 00:01:41.359
He didn't want to make Becky more afraid than she already was.

29
00:01:41.379 --> 00:01:42.879
Then he said, "I think I can find a way out, but I need some more luck."

30
00:01:42.899 --> 00:01:44.240
He leaned forward and kissed Becky.

31
00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.680
Then he crawled down a different passage.

32
00:01:49.941 --> 00:01:52.142
Kissing Becky had indeed brought Tom some luck.

33
00:01:54.522 --> 00:01:59.744
Soon Tom saw light again, but this was a different kind of light—sunlight shining through a small hole.

34
00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:06.589
Tom took out his knife and gradually made the hole big enough to squeeze through.

35
00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:13.291
After Tom and Becky climbed out of the cave, Tom covered the hole with some leaves.

36
00:02:14.252 --> 00:02:17.172
He didn't want Injun Joe to find it and escape the same way.

37
00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:24.415
When Tom realized where they were, he exclaimed, "Gosh, we're five miles downriver from town!

38
00:02:25.515 --> 00:02:28.076
We walked almost two miles underground."

39
00:02:29.568 --> 00:02:33.449
Tom and Becky walked to the river and got a barge that was headed upriver to stop for

40
00:02:33.469 --> 00:02:38.931
them. The crew on the barge had heard about the missing children, so they agreed to take them

41
00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:43.032
home. The town rejoiced, and then the two children were put to bed.

42
00:02:43.793 --> 00:02:47.854
Becky stayed in bed for almost four days, but Tom felt better after two.

43
00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:53.156
Tom learned that Huck had been sick as well, so Tom went to visit his friend at the

44
00:02:53.196 --> 00:02:53.956
Welshman's house.

45
00:02:55.436 --> 00:03:00.119
When Tom and Huck were alone, Tom told Huck that he thought he knew where the treasure was.

46
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.062
Huck shook his head and said, "It isn't in the tavern, Tom."

47
00:03:04.963 --> 00:03:08.025
Tom wanted to interrupt his friend, but Huck was talking too fast.

48
00:03:08.045 --> 00:03:13.489
"When I was sick," said Huck, "I dreamed a lot, and I guess I did a lot of

49
00:03:13.529 --> 00:03:19.193
talking. I talked about the tavern, I talked about Injun Joe and the murder, and I talked about

50
00:03:19.213 --> 00:03:20.013
the Widow Douglas.

51
00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:23.696
The Welshman and others figured things out and searched the tavern.

52
00:03:24.312 --> 00:03:25.633
But all they found was whiskey."

53
00:03:26.853 --> 00:03:27.653
Tom smiled.

54
00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.054
"Of course!

55
00:03:29.754 --> 00:03:32.375
That's all they found because the gold is in the cave.

56
00:03:33.176 --> 00:03:35.057
I saw Injun Joe in the cave."

57
00:03:36.577 --> 00:03:41.179
"The night you were found, Judge Thatcher blocked the cave entrance with an iron door," said Huck.

58
00:03:41.199 --> 00:03:44.461
"He didn't want what happened to you and Becky to happen again."

59
00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.082
Tom wanted to go to the judge.

60
00:03:48.062 --> 00:03:52.064
But the Widow Douglas, who had been taking care of Huck at the Welshman's house, wouldn't let Huck

61
00:03:52.124 --> 00:03:57.310
go. So Tom went by himself, and then headed back to the cave with the judge and the

62
00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:00.631
sheriff. The judge opened the great iron door with his key.

63
00:04:01.571 --> 00:04:04.773
Inside they found Injun Joe lying dead on the ground.

64
00:04:06.173 --> 00:04:09.415
His knife was broken at his side where he had tried to chip his way out.

65
00:04:10.975 --> 00:04:12.436
The next day Tom got Huck.

66
00:04:13.376 --> 00:04:15.637
They borrowed a rowboat, and Tom rowed downriver.

67
00:04:16.738 --> 00:04:19.019
Tom found his secret entrance to the cave easily.

68
00:04:19.039 --> 00:04:21.460
They each lit a candle and entered.

69
00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:28.061
Tom showed Huck where he and Becky had slept, and then he led Huck to where he had

70
00:04:28.121 --> 00:04:28.921
seen Injun Joe.

71
00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.222
They climbed down into the chamber.

72
00:04:31.962 --> 00:04:36.543
Tom and Huck both noticed the large cross on the wall, and they immediately started digging.

73
00:04:37.184 --> 00:04:39.544
They didn't have to dig long before they came to a board.

74
00:04:41.685 --> 00:04:44.666
They lifted the board, and under it was a small compartment.

75
00:04:45.686 --> 00:04:51.187
Inside the compartment were some candles, some matches, and a box full of silver and gold.

76
00:04:51.207 --> 00:04:53.628
"Finally!" exclaimed Huck.

77
00:04:54.304 --> 00:04:55.506
"We found the treasure!"

78
00:04:55.526 --> 00:05:01.033
"Even when money's free," said Tom, "you still have to work for it."
